杰森:你不必这样的.
Jason: Well that wasn't necessary.

365
00:21:38,200 --> 00:21:41,040
麦琪:幸运的是,我最后接受了那个专栏.
Maggie: Fortunately the part of me that spoke accepted the column.

366
00:21:41,900 --> 00:21:44,180
但我正告他对你太无理了.
But I did tell hi I resented the way he treated you.

367
00:21:44,580 --> 00:21:47,260
杰森:他是很粗鲁,是不是?但他是对的.
Jason: Well he was blunt, wasn't he, but he was right.

368
00:21:48,520 --> 00:21:53,500
我看了你的文章,麦琪.没有模糊术语,
I got a copy of your article Maggie, no buzzwords, no passive sentences,

369
00:21:53,580 --> 00:21:55,700
没有被动句.你的文字敏锐,
only sharp, intelligent, funny.

370
00:21:55,740 --> 00:21:59,460
机智,有趣,让我想起了跟佛里德伊斯泰尔跳舞的那个晚上.
Reminded me of the night I danced with Fred Estair.

371
00:22:01,200 --> 00:22:03,080
麦琪:你从没跟佛里德伊斯泰尔跳过舞.
